  "content": {
    "id": "p30-stem-49-54",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Solve the following for $0^{\\circ}\\leq\\theta\\leq360^{\\circ}$.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p30-q49",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\sin^2\\theta=1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=90^{\\circ},\\ 270^{\\circ}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\sin^2\\theta&=1\\\\\\sin\\theta&=\\pm1\\\\\\theta&=90^{\\circ},\\ 270^{\\circ}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q50",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\cos^2\\theta=\\frac34$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=30^{\\circ},\\ 150^{\\circ},\\ 210^{\\circ},\\ 330^{\\circ}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\cos^2\\theta&=\\frac34\\\\\\cos\\theta&=\\pm\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\end{align*}$$\nThe related angle is $30^{\\circ}$. Both signs include all four quadrants.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=30^{\\circ},\\ 180^{\\circ}-30^{\\circ},\\ 180^{\\circ}+30^{\\circ},\\ 360^{\\circ}-30^{\\circ}\\\\\\theta&=30^{\\circ},\\ 150^{\\circ},\\ 210^{\\circ},\\ 330^{\\circ}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q51",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\tan^2\\theta=3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=60^{\\circ},\\ 120^{\\circ},\\ 240^{\\circ},\\ 300^{\\circ}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\tan^2\\theta&=3\\\\\\tan\\theta&=\\pm\\sqrt3\\end{align*}$$\nThe related angle is $60^{\\circ}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan\\theta=\\sqrt3:\\quad\\theta&=60^{\\circ},\\ 240^{\\circ}\\\\\\tan\\theta=-\\sqrt3:\\quad\\theta&=120^{\\circ},\\ 300^{\\circ}\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore $\\theta=60^{\\circ},\\ 120^{\\circ},\\ 240^{\\circ},\\ 300^{\\circ}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q52",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$2\\cos^2\\theta-1=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=45^{\\circ},\\ 135^{\\circ},\\ 225^{\\circ},\\ 315^{\\circ}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2\\cos^2\\theta-1&=0\\\\2\\cos^2\\theta&=1\\\\\\cos^2\\theta&=\\frac12\\\\\\cos\\theta&=\\pm\\frac1{\\sqrt2}\\end{align*}$$\nThe related angle is $45^{\\circ}$. Both signs include all four quadrants.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=45^{\\circ},\\ 135^{\\circ},\\ 225^{\\circ},\\ 315^{\\circ}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 62
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q53",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$3\\tan^2\\theta-1=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=30^{\\circ},\\ 150^{\\circ},\\ 210^{\\circ},\\ 330^{\\circ}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}3\\tan^2\\theta-1&=0\\\\3\\tan^2\\theta&=1\\\\\\tan^2\\theta&=\\frac13\\\\\\tan\\theta&=\\pm\\frac1{\\sqrt3}\\end{align*}$$\nThe related angle is $30^{\\circ}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan\\theta=\\frac1{\\sqrt3}:\\quad\\theta&=30^{\\circ},\\ 210^{\\circ}\\\\\\tan\\theta=-\\frac1{\\sqrt3}:\\quad\\theta&=150^{\\circ},\\ 330^{\\circ}\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore $\\theta=30^{\\circ},\\ 150^{\\circ},\\ 210^{\\circ},\\ 330^{\\circ}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 72
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q54",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$2\\sin^2\\theta+\\sin\\theta-1=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=30^{\\circ},\\ 150^{\\circ},\\ 270^{\\circ}$.\n\nFactor as $(2\\sin\\theta-1)(\\sin\\theta+1)=0$ and solve both branches.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2\\sin^2\\theta+\\sin\\theta-1&=0\\\\(2\\sin\\theta-1)(\\sin\\theta+1)&=0\\\\\\sin\\theta&=\\frac12\\ \\text{or}\\ -1\\end{align*}$$\nFor $\\sin\\theta=\\frac12$, the related angle is $30^{\\circ}$ and sine is positive in quadrants 1 and 2:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=30^{\\circ},\\ 180^{\\circ}-30^{\\circ}\\\\\\theta&=30^{\\circ},\\ 150^{\\circ}\\end{align*}$$\nFor $\\sin\\theta=-1$, $\\theta=270^{\\circ}$.\nTherefore $\\theta=30^{\\circ},\\ 150^{\\circ},\\ 270^{\\circ}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 70
      }
    ]
  },
